# Star Wars
A guide to the galaxy, what it draws and does.  Every thing it shows is in StarWars.api.spell, as `spell place ingest` wrote it:
say what a field links to, and reading it follows the link, `the name of its homeworld`.
Each type below adds to its type there, with `<extend>`:  so looking again at the server never touches a line of this.

<app "guide">
	<spell>
		- its "tab" is text
		- its "search" is text
		- to create it:
			set its tab to "films"
			set its search to ""
		- its "showing" is a thing
		- its "trail" is a new list of things
		- its "playing" is a film
		- its "jumping" is yes or no
	</spell>

	<property "found" description="Whatever's found:  the film, character, planet, ship or anything else with that in its name">
		set matches to a new list of things
		for film in every film where its title includes the guide's search
			add the film to matches
		for character in every character where its name includes the guide's search
			add the character to matches
		for planet in every planet where its name includes the guide's search
			add the planet to matches
		for starship in every starship where its name includes the guide's search
			add the starship to matches
		for vehicle in every vehicle where its name includes the guide's search
			add the vehicle to matches
		for one in every species where its name includes the guide's search
			add the one to matches
		return matches
	</property>

	<action "go back">
		if its trail is empty
			set its showing to nothing
			return
		set its showing to the last item of its trail
		remove the last item of its trail
		scroll to the top
	</action>

	<action "go to (where as text)">
		set its tab to where
		set its search to ""
		set its showing to nothing
		clear its trail
		scroll to the top
	</action>

	<action "play the opening">
		set its playing to the first film
	</action>

	<action "punch it" description="A jump to light speed, and wherever it lands">
		set its jumping to yes
		set landing to a random character in (every character)
		pause for 2600 msec
		open landing
		set its jumping to no
	</action>

	<draw>
		<if its jumping>
			draw (a new jump)
		</if>
		<stack direction="horizontal" wrap align="end" justify="between">
			<button class="logo" appearance="transparent" font="all-caps" onClick={go to "films"}>Star Wars</button>
			<form value={it} class="find">
				<field label="Search the galaxy">
					<input name="search" icon="search" placeholder="Luke, Hoth, Falcon"/>
				</field>
			</form>
			<button class="punch" color="primary" font="all-caps" onClick={punch it} title="Jump to light speed, and land on someone">Punch it</button>
		</stack>
		<toolbar appearance="secondary pointing" aria-label="Browse">
			<item active={its tab is "films"} onClick={go to "films"}>Films</item>
			<item active={its tab is "characters"} onClick={go to "characters"}>Characters</item>
			<item active={its tab is "planets"} onClick={go to "planets"}>Planets</item>
			<item active={its tab is "ships"} onClick={go to "ships"}>Ships</item>
			<item active={its tab is "vehicles"} onClick={go to "vehicles"}>Vehicles</item>
			<item active={its tab is "species"} onClick={go to "species"}>Species</item>
		</toolbar>
		draw its shelf
		<text paragraph size="small">
			Films, characters, planets and ships from <link link="https://swapi.py4e.com/">swapi.py4e.com</link>.
			Pictures and what they're of from <link link="https://en.wikipedia.org/">Wikipedia</link>, asked for as you look.
			Star Wars belongs to Lucasfilm and Disney.
		</text>
		<if its playing>
			draw the crawl of its playing
		</if>
	</draw>

	<draw "shelf" description="Each tab's list says nothing of how long it is:  a long one draws what fits, and more as you scroll">
		<if its showing and its search is "">
			draw its showing's page
		<otherwise if its search is not "">
			<header size="medium">Searching for “{its search}”</header>
			<for its found as="cards" columns="4" doubling loading={its signal} failed={its lost signal} empty="Nobody and nothing by that name, in this galaxy." />
		<otherwise if its tab is "films">
			<segment class="opening" inverted align="center">
				<text class="long-ago" size="large">A long time ago in a galaxy far, far away....</text>
				<button class="play-opening" size="massive" font="all-caps" onClick={play the opening of the guide}>Play the opening</button>
			</segment>
			<for every film as="cards" columns="4" doubling loading={its signal} failed={its lost signal} />
		<otherwise if its tab is "characters">
			<for every character as="cards" columns="4" doubling loading={its signal} failed={its lost signal} />
		<otherwise if its tab is "planets">
			<for every planet as="cards" columns="4" doubling loading={its signal} failed={its lost signal} />
		<otherwise if its tab is "vehicles">
			<for every vehicle as="cards" columns="4" doubling loading={its signal} failed={its lost signal} />
		<otherwise if its tab is "species">
			<for every species as="cards" columns="4" doubling loading={its signal} failed={its lost signal} />
		<otherwise>
			<for every starship as="cards" columns="4" doubling loading={its signal} failed={its lost signal} />
		</>
	</draw>

	<property "signal">"Waiting for a signal from the galaxy"</property>
	<property "lost signal">"The signal from swapi.py4e.com is lost."</property>
</app>


# What everything here can do
It's on `a thing`, not a base type of the program's own:  each type below is simply `a thing`.
Spell has no mixins yet (epic `mixins`), and a thing here shares by HOLDING a card, and drawing it.

<spell>
	to open (a thing):
		if the guide's showing
			add the guide's showing to the guide's trail
		set the guide's search to ""
		set the guide's showing to it
		scroll to the top

	// A number for people to read:  with none, nothing, so its row doesn't show
	to measure (amount as a number) in (unit as text):
		if amount is nothing
			return ""
		return amount with commas + " " + unit
</spell>


# A card:  a picture, a name, what kind, and a click anywhere on it opens the thing
Every type holds one of these, with its own words.

<thing "card">
	<property "label" />
	<property "kind" />
	<property "shape" />
	<property "colour" description="What colour a picture's background is:  from its name, unless it says" />
	<property "hue">
		if its colour is not nothing
			return its colour
		return the length of its label * 47
	</property>
	<spell>
		- its "subject" is a thing
		- its "species" is a species
	</spell>

	<draw>
		<ui-card onClick={open its subject}>
			{draw its portrait}
			<content>
				<header>{its label}</header>
				<meta>{its kind}</meta>
			</content>
		</ui-card>
	</draw>

	<draw "portrait">
		draw (a new portrait with name = its label, hue = its hue, shape = its shape, species = its species)
	</draw>

	<draw "top">
		<button appearance="transparent" icon="arrow left" onClick={go back}>Back</button>
		<stack class="hero" direction="horizontal" wrap align="start">
			{draw its portrait}
			<stack class="about">
				<header class="title" font="all-caps">{its label}</header>
				<text color="grey">{its kind}</text>
				{draw (a new wiki note with name = its label)}
			</stack>
		</stack>
	</draw>
</thing>


# What Wikipedia says of it, and where to read the rest
Not every name has a page, and a name may be someone else's:  Zolan is a medicine.

<extend "wiki page">
	<property "fits">
		if its title includes "List of"
			return no
		return its about includes "star wars" or its about includes "fictional" or its about includes " film "
	</property>
</extend>

<thing "wiki note">
	<property "name" />
	<property "page">the wiki page whose id is its name</property>
	<draw>
		draw its words
		while waiting:
			<text color="grey">Asking Wikipedia</text>
		if that fails:
			<text color="grey">Wikipedia can't be reached just now.</text>
	</draw>
	<draw "words">
		<if its page and its page's fits>
			<text paragraph>{its page's summary} <link link={the page of the desktop of the content urls of its page} target="_blank">Read the rest on Wikipedia</link></text>
		</if>
	</draw>
</thing>


# A page's parts
A table of what's known, leaving out what isn't;  a list under its heading, or nothing if it's empty.

<thing "fact">
	<property "label" />
	<property "value" />
	<spell>
		- its "date" is a date
	</spell>
	<alias "is known" description="What a server writes when nothing's known isn't worth a row">
		if its date
			return yes
		if its value is nothing or its value is ""
			return no
		return its value is not "unknown" and its value is not "n/a" and its value is not "none"
	</alias>
	<draw>
		<row>
			<cell header>{its label}</cell>
			<cell>{its value}{its date}</cell>
		</row>
	</draw>
</thing>

<thing "fact table">
	<spell>
		- its "facts" is a list of facts
	</spell>
	<property "shown">the facts in its facts where it is known</property>
	<draw>
		<if its shown is not empty>
			<table class="facts" appearance="very-basic" inverted unstackable>
				{draw each fact in its shown}
			</table>
		</if>
	</draw>
</thing>

<thing "section">
	<property "heading" />
	<spell>
		- its "things" is a list of things
		- its "single" is a thing
	</spell>
	<draw>
		<if its single>
			<header class="section" size="small" font="all-caps">{its heading}</header>
			<cards columns="4" doubling>{draw its single}</cards>
		<otherwise>
			<for its things title={its heading} as="cards" columns="4" doubling hide-empty />
		</>
	</draw>
</thing>


# A film

<extend "film">
	<property "card">a new card with label = its title, kind = "Episode " + its episode id, subject = it</property>
	<action "play it">
		set the guide's playing to it
	</action>
	<action "end it">
		set the guide's playing to nothing
	</action>

	<draw>
		draw its card
	</draw>

	<property "facts">
		set known to a new list of facts
		add (a new fact with label = "Directed by", value = its director) to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Produced by", value = its producer) to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Released", date = its release date) to known
		return known
	</property>

	<draw "page">
		draw the top of its card
		<button class="play-opening" font="all-caps" onClick={play it}>Play the opening</button>
		draw (a new fact table with facts = its facts)
		draw its links
		while waiting:
			<loader visible inline text>Following the links</loader>
	</draw>

	<draw "links">
		draw (a new section with heading = "Who's in it", things = its characters)
		draw (a new section with heading = "Where it happens", things = its planets)
		draw (a new section with heading = "What they fly", things = its starships)
	</draw>

</extend>


# A character

<extend "character">
	<property "card">a new card with label = its name, kind = "Born " + its birth year, subject = it</property>
	<property "page">the wiki page whose id is its name</property>
	<property "picture" description="Their own picture on Wikipedia, or nothing">
		if its page and its page's fits and its page's thumbnail
			return its page's thumbnail's source
		return ""
	</property>

	<draw>
		draw its card
	</draw>

	<property "facts">
		set known to a new list of facts
		add (a new fact with label = "Height", value = "[its height]") to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Mass", value = "[its mass]") to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Born", value = its birth year) to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Hair", value = its hair color) to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Eyes", value = its eye color) to known
		return known
	</property>

	<draw "page">
		draw the top of its card
		draw (a new fact table with facts = its facts)
		draw its links
		while waiting:
			<loader visible inline text>Following the links</loader>
	</draw>

	<draw "links">
		draw (a new section with heading = "Home", single = its homeworld)
		draw (a new section with heading = "Films", things = its films)
		draw (a new section with heading = "What they are", things = its species)
		draw (a new section with heading = "What they fly", things = its starships)
		draw (a new section with heading = "What they drive", things = its vehicles)
	</draw>
</extend>


# A planet

<extend "planet">
	<property "card">a new card with label = its name, kind = its climate, shape = "world", colour = its hue, subject = it</property>
	<property "hue" description="What colour a world is, from its weather">
		if its climate includes "frozen"
			return 200
		if its climate includes "arid"
			return 38
		if its climate includes "murky" or its climate includes "polluted"
			return 95
		if its climate includes "tropical" or its climate includes "temperate"
			return 130 + the length of its name * 9
		return 280
	</property>

	<draw>
		draw its card
	</draw>

	<property "facts">
		set known to a new list of facts
		add (a new fact with label = "Climate", value = its climate) to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Terrain", value = its terrain) to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Diameter", value = "[its diameter]") to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Population", value = measure its population in "people") to known
		add (a new fact with label = "A day", value = measure its rotation period in "hours") to known
		add (a new fact with label = "A year", value = measure its orbital period in "days") to known
		return known
	</property>

	<draw "page">
		draw the top of its card
		draw (a new fact table with facts = its facts)
		draw its links
		while waiting:
			<loader visible inline text>Following the links</loader>
	</draw>

	<draw "links">
		draw (a new section with heading = "Who's from here", things = its residents)
		draw (a new section with heading = "Seen in", things = its films)
	</draw>
</extend>


# A ship, and a vehicle:  much the same to look at
Their pages share `to draw a craft`'s words, handed what differs.

<thing "craft page">
	<property "model" />
	<property "maker" />
	<spell>
		- its "length" is a length in m
	</spell>
	<property "crew" />
	<property "passengers" />
	<property "cost" />
	<property "x-wings long" description="How long it is, in something you can picture:  an X-wing is 12.5 metres">
		if its length is nothing
			return nothing
		return round (its length / 12.5)
	</property>
	<property "facts">
		set known to a new list of facts
		add (a new fact with label = "Model", value = its model) to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Made by", value = its maker) to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Length", value = "[its length]") to known
		add (a new fact with label = "As long as", value = measure its x-wings long in "X-wings") to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Crew", value = its crew) to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Passengers", value = measure its passengers in "people") to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Costs", value = measure its cost in "credits") to known
		return known
	</property>
	<draw>
		draw (a new fact table with facts = its facts)
	</draw>
</thing>

<extend "starship">
	<property "card">a new card with label = its name, kind = its starship class, subject = it</property>
	<draw>
		draw its card
	</draw>
	<draw "page">
		draw the top of its card
		draw (a new craft page with model = its model, maker = its manufacturer, length = its length, crew = its crew, passengers = its passengers, cost = its cost in credits)
		draw its links
		while waiting:
			<loader visible inline text>Following the links</loader>
	</draw>
	<draw "links">
		draw (a new section with heading = "Who flew it", things = its pilots)
		draw (a new section with heading = "Seen in", things = its films)
	</draw>
</extend>

<extend "vehicle">
	<property "card">a new card with label = its name, kind = its vehicle class, subject = it</property>
	<draw>
		draw its card
	</draw>
	<draw "page">
		draw the top of its card
		draw (a new craft page with model = its model, maker = its manufacturer, length = its length, crew = its crew, passengers = its passengers, cost = its cost in credits)
		draw its links
		while waiting:
			<loader visible inline text>Following the links</loader>
	</draw>
	<draw "links">
		draw (a new section with heading = "Who flew it", things = its pilots)
		draw (a new section with heading = "Seen in", things = its films)
	</draw>
</extend>


# A species
A species with no picture takes the first of its people who has one.

<extend "species">
	<property "card">a new card with label = its name, kind = its classification, subject = it, species = it</property>
	<property "picture" description="Its first character's picture:  asking for everyone at once costs one read, and each link then asks nothing">
		set everyone to every character
		set found to ""
		for character in its people
			if found is ""
				set found to the character's picture
		return found
	</property>
	<draw>
		draw its card
	</draw>

	<property "facts">
		set known to a new list of facts
		add (a new fact with label = "Language", value = its language) to known
		add (a new fact with label = "Lives for", value = its average lifespan) to known
		return known
	</property>

	<draw "page">
		draw the top of its card
		draw (a new fact table with facts = its facts)
		draw its links
		while waiting:
			<loader visible inline text>Following the links</loader>
	</draw>

	<draw "links">
		draw (a new section with heading = "Home", single = its homeworld)
		draw (a new section with heading = "Who's one", things = its people)
	</draw>
</extend>


<spell>
	start the guide
</spell>
